  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="562df54b-a2c7-5e1e-98ea-d6a8aa44984a" activityNameId="902eba04-c56e-5e56-bf18-ecda20b9cb60" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, ventilation system for appartment buildings, steel ducts, without GHE</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, ventilation system for appartment buildings, steel ducts, without GHE
Disposal of a ventilation system for an appartment building with a specific air flow rate of 0.92 m3/h per m2 heated gross floor area. The reference value of the inventory is 1 m2 heated gross floor area. The inventory is based on a study of an appartment building with 6 flats, a heated gross floor area of 780 m2 and a total nominal air flow of 720 m3/h. The inventory includes an average of decentral and central systems. It includes average components for air handling units, ducts (including 30mm thermal insulation where needed), air valves, roof-hoods, dampers and silencers. No insuation for fire protection or fire dampers included. The data represent a ductwork mainly made of galvanized steel and includes compact air handling units with cross plate heat excangers as heat recovery and a nominal air flow rate of 200-1200 m3/h per unit. No ground heat exchanger, ventilation of side rooms, cellars or car parks are included.;
UUID: 62698e20-cc0e-4926-b549-73a47a009d0e
Transport to dismantling facilities, machines for handling in sorting plant, electricity demand for sorting plant, final disposal of waste material. Cut-off to recycling for metals.
Location: Specific to the technology mix encountered in sorting plants in Switzerland.
Technology: Disposal to a sorting plant assumed. Metal pieces, copper in cables and electronic devices are recycled, plastic parts are incinerated, inert wastes (e.g. rock wool) are landfilled.
Time period: Amount of material investigated in 2003. Process information partly from 2008. Disposal technology mix as used in late 1990ies
Production volume: na
Sampling: Waste-specific calculation based on production input data 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_62698e20-cc0e-4926-b549-73a47a009d0e.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="fdab769f-4bdb-5024-8349-c1745bbb2597" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
